# UI / Components

> Adjust the globs above to match the repo's actual folder layout.

- Use the shadcn/ui + Radix primitives already in the repo. Do not add a competing
  component or styling library.
- Forms use react-hook-form; follow the existing validation pattern (e.g. a zod resolver
  if one is already used).
- Charts use Recharts.
- Gate every action-triggering control on the RBAC permission for that resource + action.
  A user lacking permission should neither see nor be able to trigger the action.
- Respect role-specific dashboard variants (Customer Relations differs from Manager/Admin,
  and an Agent view is being added). When adding a widget, decide explicitly which roles see it.
- Keep tables/lists usable on typical ops datasets and the layout responsive
  (overlay sidebar on small screens).
